anizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"subscribed","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2020-07-14T18:50:38Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/658403240","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/11764#issuecomment-658403240","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/11764","id":658403240,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDY1ODQwMzI0MA==","user":{"login":"ericfelly","id":12628882,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjI4ODgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12628882?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly","html_url":"https://github.com/ericfelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-07-14T20:43:31Z","updated_at":"2020-07-14T20:43:31Z","body":"I believe I understand what's going on here.\r\n\r\nWe have a feature to report successful output groups of top-level targets even if other output groups in the same top-level target failed. This is relatively new. We have a bug here where we're not appropriately applying path transformation to the \"remote\" filesystem related to --experimental_remote_download_outputs=minimal. When we go to upload the properly built output file, we're improperly consulting the _local_ filesystem where it will not be present.\r\n\r\nA similar issue occurs in Blaze, but we're more tolerant to missing files in that case. Here, we fail to upload the file, which fails the BES upload, and that triggers a follow-on threadpool crash.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/658403240/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ericfelly","id":12628882,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjI4ODgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12628882?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly","html_url":"https://github.com/ericfelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericfelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/658404032","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/11764#issuecomment-658404032","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/11764","id":658